    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup configuration headlined by **Trea Turner** (75.42), whose elite speed profile and favorable matchup against Kyle Freeland make him our primary engine for Stolen Bases and run production. **Kyle Schwarber** (71.37) joins him as a priority start, capitalizing on the same soft matchup with a high xwOBA that suggests a multi-hit potential. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.15) provides high-upside utility today; despite batting 8th, his dynamic platoon advantage against Jack Leiter combined with a 94% SB probability against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him an essential piece of our pursuit for category scarcity. **Colt Keith** (67.35) and **Junior Caminero** (66.72) also project as strong starts, benefiting significantly from park factors and favorable platoon splits against their respective opposing starters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Chase Meidroth** (51.75), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Luke Raley** (52.31). While **Chase Meidroth** offered a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the wind-aided boost and park conditions favoring **Luke Raley**, even though the latter faces a slight negative platoon split. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Zac Veen**, all of whom remain unavailable due to injury or minor league assignment, putting further pressure on our depth pieces like **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.93) to sustain production. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (61.66); while his elite raw talent is undeniable, he faces a daunting matchup against a high-tier arm, which drags his efficiency score down despite his immense base projection. Managers should keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Carson Benge**, **Luke Raley**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, as any adjustments to the batting order\u2014specifically for **Gary Sanchez** or **Hyeseong Kim**\u2014could force a late-inning pivot to protect our efficiency margins.",
